      "id": "finite-difference-derivatives-r1-q1",
      "round": 1,
      "type": "mc",
      "prompt": "The forward difference of a scalar function at \\(x\\) with step \\(h > 0\\) is",
      "explanation": "The forward difference uses one neighbor on the positive side and divides by the step. Dividing by \\(2h\\) belongs to the central difference, and the central difference also samples the other neighbor. Omitting the division leaves a change in value, not a slope. The central numerator over a single \\(h\\) is twice a slope.",
