      "prompt": "Put these steps in the order used to choose a finite-difference step.",
      "explanation": "Truncation falls as the step shrinks, and round-off of a difference quotient grows. The useful step is near where those two contributions meet. Shrinking past that point makes the computed slope worse. Evaluating the function once, with no error model, does not choose a step.",
